# Site Content Module Implementation Guide

## Objective

Implement a scalable **Site Content** module that allows administrators to manage all static website pages from the Admin Panel and automatically reflects the latest content on the Website.

The module will initially contain:

- About Us
- Privacy Policy
- Terms of Service
The architecture should be extensible so additional pages (FAQ, Disclaimer, Careers, etc.) can be added later without changing the overall implementation.

---

# General Rules

- Never break any existing functionality.
- Never modify unrelated modules.
- Follow existing project architecture.
- Reuse existing layouts, components and services.
- Follow existing coding standards.
- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Avoid duplicate code.
- Build reusable components.
- Keep API layer separate from UI.
- Handle Loading, Error and Empty states.
- Responsive implementation is mandatory.
- Accessibility should not be broken.

---

