# ADMIN IMPLEMENTATION

## Menu

Create a new sidebar module:

```
Site Content
```

Submenus

```
About Us
Privacy Policy
Terms of Service
```

Do NOT hardcode menu items.

Use existing sidebar architecture.

---

# Admin Pages

Each submenu opens its own page.

Each page should contain:

- Title
- Rich Text Editor
- Save Button
- Cancel Button

If project already has a reusable editor,

Reuse it.

Do NOT introduce another editor package.

---

# Fields

Every page contains

```
Title

Content

Status
```

Status

- Active
- Inactive

---

# Rich Text Support

# Validation

Title

- Required

Content

- Required

Show validation messages using existing UI.

---

# Save Behaviour

On Save

- Validate form
- Call API
- Show Success Toast
- Stay on same page

On Failure

- Show API error
- Preserve entered content

---

# Unsaved Changes

If user navigates away

Show confirmation dialog

if there are unsaved changes.

---

# API Layer

Do NOT call APIs directly inside components.

Use

```
services/
api/
hooks/
```

as per project architecture.

---

# Loading State

While fetching

Show existing loader/skeleton.

---

# Error State

Show reusable error component.

---

# Empty State

If page has no content

Show empty editor.

Do not inject dummy text.

---

# WEB IMPLEMENTATION

## Objective

Website pages should fetch content dynamically from backend.

Never hardcode content.

---

# Pages

```
/about-us

/privacy-policy

/terms-of-service
```
and link all these pages with respective navlink in Footer.
---

# Rendering

Fetch content from backend.

Render HTML safely.

Reuse existing HTML renderer if available.

Do not use dangerouslySetInnerHTML unless project already follows that pattern.

---

# SEO

Each page should support

- Title
- Meta Title
- Meta Description
- Canonical URL (if supported)
- Open Graph (if existing)

Reuse current SEO implementation.

---

# Dynamic Metadata

Metadata should come from API whenever supported.

Fallback to existing default SEO.

---

# Loading

While fetching

Show skeleton.

---

# Error

If API fails

Show reusable error screen.

---

# Empty Content

If backend returns empty content

Show reusable empty state.

Do not show lorem ipsum.

---

# Responsive

Desktop

Tablet

Mobile

must match existing design system.

---

# Performance

- Lazy load heavy editor components.
- Minimize re-renders.
- Cache requests if project already uses React Query/SWR.
- Avoid unnecessary API calls.

---

# Security

Sanitize rendered HTML.

Prevent XSS.

Never trust API HTML blindly.

---

# Future Scalability

The implementation must support adding new pages simply by:

1. Creating new record in backend
2. Adding menu entry
3. No major frontend code changes

Avoid switch-case implementations for every page.

Prefer reusable page configuration.

---

# Suggested API Structure

List Pages

```
GET /site-content
```

Single Page

```
GET /site-content/{slug}
```

Update

```
PUT /site-content/{slug}
```

Example slugs

```
about-us

privacy-policy

terms-of-service
```

---

# Suggested Response

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Privacy Policy",
  "slug": "privacy-policy",
  "content": "<p>...</p>",
  "status": "active",
  "updatedAt": ""
}
```

---

# Reusability

Create reusable:

- SiteContentEditor
- SiteContentForm
- SiteContentService
- SiteContentRenderer
- SiteContentSkeleton
- SiteContentError
- SiteContentEmpty

Avoid page-specific duplicated components.

